# fixedbugs, defect 2253, 2026-10-29: one call past a line the program
# printed, into a function whose frame is larger than what is left of the
# stack, which died at 139 with nothing on stderr (the case of `main` beside
# this one says how, and what repaired it). The line must survive the abort:
# it is printed before the call, and the stop is the callee's own prologue,
# in `fixedbugs2253/held`, a module whose unit is its own so `-O2` keeps the
# call a call. Darwin and Linux name `held.kept`; Windows' guard names no
# function and says the first sentence alone.
use fixedbugs2253/held

function main()
    print("printed before the call")
    print(held.kept(n: 7))
